# Line endings, in one rule rather than per suffix.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` was checking these files out as CRLF while the index held LF, so
# `git ls-files --eol` reported `i/lf w/crlf` on 75 of 323 files. Nothing was wrong in the
# index and nothing needed renormalizing -- the damage was confined to the working tree,
# where it surfaces as spurious diffs and as tools that read a stray carriage return as
# part of a value.
#
# A suffix list is what failed the previous five times: it answers for the extensions
# somebody remembered and stays silent about the rest. `*` cannot be incomplete.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Detected as binary already; named so the rule above can never be asked about them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
